Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:10:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Honor scheduled departure in EasyFullControl

ExecutePlan preserves planned waypoint times, but EasyFullControl previously
issued each navigation callback immediately when the preceding callback
finished. A collapsed wait only increased planned_wait_time, and that value was
used solely by arrival_estimator. Therefore a collision-free joint plan could
contain a deliberate bay/holding wait while the physical command stream left
the wait early.

Gate each navigation command asynchronously on its source waypoint's planned
departure time. When a collapsed wait is folded into a command, also defer that
command's completion until the folded wait end so a final wait cannot disappear.
A command cancelled before its scheduled departure has never been sent to the
robot, so cancellation invalidates the activity and timer without issuing a
duplicate robot stop. Existing make_hold/localization/lift waits are unchanged.

No solver, planning budget, or agent-count policy changes.
